course: dictionary
lesson: 13083
title: Figurative language
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Figurative means the words do not mean exactly what they say. Writers use it to paint a picture in your mind. «The classroom was a zoo after the bell.» Nobody found real animals in the classroom. It means it was noisy and wild.
explain: Ask yourself: could this be true word for word? If not, the words are figurative. «Her heart is a lion» cannot be true word for word, so read it for its meaning, brave and fierce, not as a body part.
explain: Figurative language includes similes, metaphors, personification and idioms. A simile uses «like» or «as», a metaphor says one thing is another, and personification gives things human feelings. Each one tells the reader not to take the words literally.
fact: Figurative means not word-for-word; it says one thing to mean another.
fact: «A heart of gold» is figurative: it means a very kind person, not a heart made of metal.
fact: «The wind whispered through the trees» is figurative: wind cannot really whisper.
fact: In art, figurative means showing real people or things you can recognise, not just abstract shapes.
fact: Literal means the exact, word-for-word meaning. It is the opposite of figurative.
exercise: What does «He has a heart of gold» mean? | He lost his heart somewhere | He is made of gold | He is very rich | *He is very kind and generous
exercise: «The sun smiled down on the picnic.» Find the figurative word. | *smiled | sun | down | picnic
exercise: Which sentence is a simile? | The moon is a silver coin | The moon is bright tonight | Moon shines | *The moon is like a silver coin
test: Is «The wind whispered through the trees» figurative or literal? | *Figurative, because wind does not really whisper | Literal, because wind really whispers | Literal, because trees can hear | Figurative, because it is about trees
test: The opposite of figurative is what? | Art | *Literal | Happy | Loud
exam: In art, what does figurative mean? | Painted in gold | Made of abstract shapes only | Drawn by a child | *Showing real people or things you can recognise
